Rejects experimental B3 selection in build, run, test, and translate before compiler or worker initialization, including with --no-verify. These commands previously accepted the B3 option but verified through Boogie instead.

Also rejects B3 in measure-complexity, generate-tests, and find-dead-code before preparation or generation. Test generation and dead-code analysis now load the backend selector from project files, so a B3 project cannot silently invoke their Boogie analysis.

Project configuration changes now retire the old IDE observer and cancel its work before replacing the manager for every open source in that project. Late results cannot overwrite replacement diagnostics. Moving a source to a different project releases its actual old source reference.

B3 now explicitly rejects nonzero editor verification caching levels before worker lookup, including for sources with no verification units. The default cache-verification level 0 remains supported.

B3 configuration accepts the native unset-cache sentinel as disabled, alongside the modern zero level; positive verification-cache levels remain explicitly unsupported.
